# Beta feature rollout

Traces to `[Corpus: adr/ADR-043]` and `[Corpus: product]` (operator-facing Fn).

## When adding a new product feature (operator UI or public-facing capability)

1. **Recommend beta** — AskQuestion first option: ship with a visible **Beta** badge/label
   and plain-language “feedback welcome” copy.
2. **Point to Issues** — Wire a feedback link to  
   `https://github.com/EMPIRIC2/TAC-to-IWXXM/issues/new?labels=beta-feedback`  
   (reuse the shared template/label; do not invent a second URL scheme without ADR).
3. **Docs** — Note beta + feedback in root `README.md` (and GitHub About when the feature is
   user-visible from the landing description).
4. **Waive only via AskQuestion** — If the feature is clearly GA on day one, record the
   waiver in `docs/decisions/` / session decisions; do not silently skip beta.

## Must not

- Put internal doc refs (`[Corpus:…]`, ADR/EV/TC ids, `docs/sessions/…`) in operator copy
  (EV-048 / `no-internal-doc-refs-user-facing.mdc`).
- Treat beta as a substitute for egress/SSRF/BYOC safety on dissemination paths.

## Related

- Issue template: `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/beta_feedback.md`
- Dissemination beta surfaces: F16–F19 (EV-1150)
- PyPI publish cadence is separate (`pypi-package-publish.mdc` / ADR-043 §B)
